  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nIssued 335 AM MST WED NOV 11 2026\nPrecipitation will taper off from the west Saturday morning as \na cold front moves east of the area. Highs will cool around 10 \ndegrees from Friday behind the front. Winds will not be as \nstrong as Friday but will still be breezy with gusts 15-30 mph \nfrom the west to northwest. An upper level ridge will briefly \nmove overhead late Saturday through most of Sunday as another \ndeep low approaches the coast. Winds will continue to be breezy\non Sunday ahead of this next system with temperatures \nrebounding a few degrees. Similar to the previous system, this \nsystem will weaken as it moves inland but bring with it a cold \nfront and precipitation. While ensembles differ on the exact \ntiming, it is expected to move through between Sunday night and\nearly Tuesday, with Monday seeing the highest (50-80%) chance \nof precipitation. Light to locally moderate precipitation totals\nare expected. Snow levels will lower from around 6000 feet \nSunday night to 4000-5500 feet by the time precipitation ends, \nallowing for additional mountain snowfall. Temperatures will \ntrend lower with highs cooling to near normal by Tuesday. Winds \nwill continue to weaken as the system progresses but remain \nlocally breezy. On Wednesday, another low from the Gulf of \nAlaska will approach the coast with precipitation chances \nincreasing late in the day.",
